  "sampling": "Exactly sixteen fresh-process samples: four same-ELF A/A pairs covering both subjects and scales, then two reversed comparison blocks per scale. Each sample 50000 sends after 5000 warmup. No extension on results.",
  "analysis": "Use existing raw verifier and descriptive paired counters; two block ratios per scale, no confidence interval or equivalence claim. Keep all CPU/cycle results even when adverse.",
  "decision": "Counter screen only: require all identities, payload checks, zero migrations and 100% counter runtime. Both scales must have median instructions/op <= -3% relative to R123 to proceed toward router performance. If any same-ELF instruction A/A pair exceeds +/-0.5%, resolve count instability before screening. These are resource-allocation heuristics, not necessary conditions for router performance gain and not language-limit evidence.",
  "boundaries": "Enable ACK after warmup before the three clock reads; disable ACK after the loop and the three clock reads. No per-request instrumentation. Final callback validates delivery; bounded trailing daemon work can straddle the CPU-clock/disable boundary. Counts include this boundary overhead and are divided by 50000.",
